{"name":"Rose Garden","hex":"#da9ec8","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose garden","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A garden devoted primarily to roses.","A highly desirable situation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose_garden"}],"entries":[{"title":"White House Rose Garden","blocks":[{"text":"The White House Rose Garden is a garden bordering the Oval Office and the West Wing of the White House in Washington, D.C., United States. The area is approximately 125 feet long and 60 feet wide. It is adjacent to the South Lawn and is commonly used as a stage for receptions and media events due to its proximity to the building."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ee/White_House_Rose_Garden.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White_House_Rose_Garden","wikidata":"Q672618"},{"title":"Rose Garden, San Jose","blocks":[{"text":"Rose Garden, also rendered as Rosegarden, is a historic district of Central San Jose, California, near Downtown San Jose and The Alameda. Rose Garden is a district made up of numerous historic neighborhoods, such as Hanchett Park, primarily characterized by its architecture and numerous cultural institutions, including the San Jose Municipal Rose Garden, Rosicrucian Park, which includes the Rosicrucian Egyptian Museum, and the historic Hoover Theater."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b1/Stores_in_Rose_Garden%2C_San_Jose_0980.jpg/330px-Stores_in_Rose_Garden%2C_San_Jose_0980.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Garden%2C_San_Jose","wikidata":"Q7367727"},{"title":"Rose Garden (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Rose Garden\" is a song written in 1967 by American singer-songwriter Joe South. It was first recorded by Billy Joe Royal on his 1967 studio album Billy Joe Royal Featuring Hush. Versions by South himself and Dobie Gray appeared shortly after the original. Gray's version became a minor hit in North America in 1969."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_Garden_(song)","wikidata":"Q158554"},{"title":"Rose garden","blocks":[{"text":"A rose garden or rosarium is a garden or park, often open to the public, used to present and grow various types of garden roses, and sometimes rose species. Designs vary tremendously and roses may be displayed alongside other plants or grouped by individual variety, colour or class in rose beds. Technically it is a specialized type of shrub garden, but normally treated as a type of flower garden, if only because its origins in Europe go back to at least the Middle Ages in Europe, when roses were effectively the largest and most popular flowers, already existing in numerous garden cultivars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Aramaki_rose_park04s2400.jpg/330px-Aramaki_rose_park04s2400.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_garden","wikidata":"Q291177"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg/500px-White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg/1280px-White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg/500px-White_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The west colonial garden in the Theodore Roosevelt era, around 1908","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AWhite_House-_West_garden_LOC_hec.14660.jpg"},{"srcset":"